## Test that profile-guided optimization preserves unmodified functions.
## When no functions have their layout changed (e.g. profile matches no hot
## edges), the output binary must be identical to the input.  This verifies
## that the MC re-encoding byte differences are NOT written back.

# RUN: yaml2obj %p/Inputs/two-funcs.yaml -o %t.exe
# RUN: printf "1 func_0x140001030 0 1 func_0x140001030 0 0 1\n" > %t.fdata
# RUN: llvm-bolt %t.exe -o %t.out.exe -data=%t.fdata -reorder-blocks=ext-tsp \
# RUN:   2>&1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: diff %t.exe %t.out.exe

# CHECK: BOLT-INFO: 0 functions had layout modified
# CHECK: BOLT-INFO: resolved relocations for 2 functions
# CHECK: BOLT-INFO: 0 functions rewritten
